# What of this dist is COMMITTED, and what is only a build by-product.
# Same convention as heif-dist-android-arm64-v8a/.gitignore (A-T4 Finding 3,
# option c): the committed tree is what a CONSUMER needs. Unlike the HEIF
# dist, lib/*.a here is NOT excluded -- these static archives ARE the shipped
# artifact (jxl.cmake's find_library() calls resolve directly against them;
# there is no shared .so this project links instead).
#
# lib/pkgconfig/, lib/cmake/ -- build-time discovery files (hwy's CMake
# package config, pkg-config .pc files) for a prefix layout that does not
# exist on the consumer's machine. native/cmake/jxl.cmake resolves every
# archive with a direct find_library(... HINTS ${JXL_LIB_HINTS}) call, never
# through find_package(hwy) or pkg-config, so these are dead weight.
# share/man/ -- man pages for the libjxl CLI tools, which are not built
# (JPEGXL_ENABLE_TOOLS=OFF) and not shipped; documentation for a program this
# tree does not ship.
# .stage/ -- the carrier's own build scratch (cloned source tree, unstripped
# intermediate .a files, captured nm/readelf assertion evidence). Reproducible
# from the pinned sources in PROVENANCE.md by re-running the producer command;
# never intended for commit.
lib/pkgconfig/
lib/cmake/
share/man/
.stage/
